<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="69703" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/IS/591/69703.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2025" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025.xml">2025</calendarYear><term id="120251" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring.xml">Spring 2025</term><subject id="IS" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/IS.xml">Information Sciences</subject><course id="591" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/IS/591.xml">Advanced Topics in Information Services</course></parents><sectionNumber>MAO</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Music Librarianship</sectionTitle><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Music Librarianship is a unique field, requiring a firm grasp of principles of music and librarianship. This course will cover a number of aspects of music librarianship, including music reference resources, collection development, formats and digital libraries. Students will read current literature on music librarianship and analyze the theoretical and practical aspects of the field through discussions, in class activities, guest lecturers in specialty areas, and written assignments.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>Open (Restricted)</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2025-01-21Z</startDate><endDate>2025-05-07Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="E4 ">Online</type><start>04:00 PM</start><end>05:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>R      </daysOfTheWeek><instructors><instructor lastName="Johnson" firstName="K">Johnson, K</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>